\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces EgoPed\xspace  architecture. The ego trajectory is encoded by a \emph  {frozen} transformer encoder into 196 per-timestep conditioning tokens. At every denoising step, the noisy latent $\mathbf  {z}_t$ is concatenated with the full 196-token ego sequence (and the timestep embedding) and jointly processed by a self-attention transformer denoiser; the latent output tokens predict the noise. Diffusion runs in the latent space of a frozen HumanML3D VAE; only the denoiser is trained. Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:xattn} ablates an alternative cross-attention denoiser.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{\method architecture. The ego trajectory is encoded by a \emph {frozen} transformer encoder into 196 per-timestep conditioning tokens. At every denoising step, the noisy latent $\mathbf {z}_t$ is concatenated with the full 196-token ego sequence (and the timestep embedding) and jointly processed by a self-attention transformer denoiser; the latent output tokens predict the noise. Diffusion runs in the latent space of a frozen HumanML3D VAE; only the denoiser is trained. Section~\ref {sec:xattn} ablates an alternative cross-attention denoiser.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
